x01-core-alignment patch 06-inheritance-resets (git apply ignores this header)

E7 item: (e) Inheritance resets and orphan Len.

SAGE26 behaviour: joining copies each progenitor galaxy whole (R/src/core_build_model.c:234) and
zeroes Cooling, Heating, QuasarModeBHaccretionMass and OutflowRate only for a Type 0 or 1 galaxy of
the first-occupied progenitor (R/src/core_build_model.c:252, :273-276), after the merged-galaxy test
(:241-245); a Type 2 galaxy is copied unchanged, even within that progenitor (:240), and a Type 0 or 1
galaxy of another progenitor becomes an orphan that keeps them (:322-337). The six SFR histories are
zeroed on the same path (:278-282). The orphan branch never assigns Len (:322-337), so an orphan
keeps its last Len (R/src/model_misc.c:112 and R/src/core_build_model.c:261 are the only Len stores). A galaxy made by
init_galaxy starts with all four at zero (R/src/model_misc.c:175-181).

Mimic behaviour replaced: copy_progenitor_galaxy (src/core/inheritance.c:23-34) runs the generated
reset_galaxy_snapshot_accumulators on every inherited copy, which zeroes every init_repeat field the
package declares (in models/sage26/model_properties.yaml these four, SAGE26's OutflowRate being the
package's SupernovaOutflowRate, and eleven other fields), and
make_orphan (src/core/inheritance.c:79-95) sets Len = 0. The six SFR histories have no init_repeat;
the package zeroes them itself with SAGE26's predicate (models/sage26/modules/
sage26_initialise_merger_clock/sage26_initialise_merger_clock.c:139-150), so they are already as
SAGE26 and not changed here.

What the patch changes: copy_progenitor_galaxy restores Cooling, Heating, QuasarModeBHaccretionMass
and SupernovaOutflowRate from the source galaxy after the generated reset, and inherit_descendant_halos
zeroes the four for a Type 0/1 row of the main branch (first-occupied progenitor) after
apply_descendant_properties; around its make_orphan call it keeps the row's Len. Every other
init_repeat field is still reset on every inherited copy, make_orphan itself is unchanged (its other
caller, module record creation, keeps Len = 0), and no type changes.

Reading for i02: yes for sage16, which declares the same four fields with init_repeat
(models/sage26 names; models/sage16/model_properties.yaml) and writes Type 2 rows: an orphan's Cooling,
Heating, QuasarModeBHaccretionMass, SupernovaOutflowRate and Len would be carried instead of reset.
As written the patch names package fields in the core, so it compiles only for a package that
declares all four; halos-only does not, and would not build with it. Its orphan Len part alone would
change halos-only's Type 2 Len output.

diff --git a/src/core/inheritance.c b/src/core/inheritance.c
index b3ab75cb..0cfe2686 100644
--- a/src/core/inheritance.c
+++ b/src/core/inheritance.c
@@ -28,6 +28,13 @@ static void copy_progenitor_galaxy(struct GalaxyPool *pool, struct Halo *target,
     target->galaxy = galaxy_pool_alloc(pool);
     memcpy(target->galaxy, source->galaxy, sizeof(struct GalaxyData));
     reset_galaxy_snapshot_accumulators(target->galaxy);
+    /* x01 (e): SAGE26 copies a progenitor galaxy whole (R/src/core_build_model.c:234) and zeroes
+     * these four only on the first-occupied Type 0/1 update (:273-276); every inherited copy
+     * keeps them here and inherit_descendant_halos() zeroes them on that update */
+    target->galaxy->Cooling = source->galaxy->Cooling;
+    target->galaxy->Heating = source->galaxy->Heating;
+    target->galaxy->QuasarModeBHaccretionMass = source->galaxy->QuasarModeBHaccretionMass;
+    target->galaxy->SupernovaOutflowRate = source->galaxy->SupernovaOutflowRate;
   } else {
     target->galaxy = NULL;
   }
@@ -175,8 +182,18 @@ int64_t inherit_descendant_halos(struct GalaxyPool *pool, struct Halo *workspace
     if (workspace[end].Type == 0 || workspace[end].Type == 1) {
       if (progenitors[i].is_main_branch) {
         apply_descendant_properties(&workspace[end], descendant);
+        /* x01 (e): SAGE26's first-occupied reset (R/src/core_build_model.c:273-276) */
+        if (workspace[end].galaxy != NULL) {
+          workspace[end].galaxy->Cooling = 0.0;
+          workspace[end].galaxy->Heating = 0.0;
+          workspace[end].galaxy->QuasarModeBHaccretionMass = 0.0;
+          workspace[end].galaxy->SupernovaOutflowRate = 0.0;
+        }
       } else {
+        /* x01 (e): SAGE26's orphan branch leaves Len unchanged (R/src/core_build_model.c:322-337) */
+        const int len = workspace[end].Len;
         make_orphan(&workspace[end]);
+        workspace[end].Len = len;
       }
     }
 
